Footer
======
The documentation site (docs-site) is not shipped to users by a Trove install. Its
npm production dependency list is only used to confirm that no copyleft licence was
missed; at generation time it listed no third-party production dependency (VitePress
is a development dependency).

Regenerate this file from the repository root:

  ./mvnw --batch-mode -pl core org.codehaus.mojo:license-maven-plugin:2.7.1:add-third-party \
    -Dlicense.excludedScopes=test,provided,system -Dlicense.outputDirectory=<out>/lic \
    -Dlicense.thirdPartyFilename=core.txt
  for d in apps/web apps/mobile docs-site; do
    (cd $d && npm ci && npx -y license-checker-rseidelsohn@5.0.1 --production --csv \
      --out <out>/lic/$(basename $d).csv)
  done

then group each list by licence, iText first, one "name version — licence" line per
component (Maven components as group:artifact:version, npm ones as name@version).
